; NilBBS setup - run this from inside the NilBBS drawer:
;     CD <where you put it>/BBS
;     Execute Setup
; It assigns BBS: to this drawer, makes the programs executable (a .zip
; can't carry AmigaDOS protection bits) and can add NilBBS to S:User-Startup.

FailAt 21
Assign BBS: ""
; the same programs Install_NilBBS protects (>NIL: - a program this version
; doesn't have is skipped quietly)
Protect >NIL: BBS:NilBBS +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:BBSNode +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:BBSCtl +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:BBSControl +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:BBSSchedule +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:BBSConfig +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:DoorCheck +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:BBSToss +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:BBSMaint +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:NilTerm +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:Doors/Guess/Guess +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:Doors/CNTest/CNTest +e
Protect >NIL: BBS:Doors/XIMTest/XIMTest +e
MakeDir >NIL: BBS:Fido BBS:Fido/Inbound BBS:Fido/Outbound BBS:Files/Import BBS:PFiles

Echo "NilBBS is in *"`CD`*"."
Ask "Start NilBBS automatically at boot (adds 4 lines to S:User-Startup)? (y/N)"
If WARN
  ; the installer's lines run BBS:NilBBS too - either kind counts.  The
  ; markers are the installer's own, so a later Install_NilBBS finds them.
  Search >NIL: S:User-Startup "BBS:NilBBS"
  If WARN
    Echo ";BEGIN NilBBS" >>S:User-Startup
    Echo "Assign BBS: *"`CD`*"" >>S:User-Startup
    Echo "Run >NIL: BBS:NilBBS QUIET" >>S:User-Startup
    Echo ";END NilBBS" >>S:User-Startup
    Echo "Added to S:User-Startup."
  Else
    Echo "S:User-Startup already starts NilBBS - left alone."
  EndIf
EndIf
Echo ""
Echo "Next steps:"
Echo "  1. Edit BBS:Config/NilBBS.cfg (BBS name, sysop, port) and"
Echo "     BBS:Config/IPFilter.cfg (put your own LAN on an allow line)."
Echo "  2. Start your TCP/IP stack, then:  Run >NIL: BBS:NilBBS"
Echo "  3. Telnet in and sign up - the FIRST account becomes the sysop."
Echo "  4. BBS:BBSConfig edits every setting; BBS:BBSControl is the live sysop"
Echo "     console; BBS:BBSCtl the Shell one."
